id: pm-m9gu9r
title: Isolate the merge SDK bundle from focused-entrypoint chunk fanout
description: Build the narrow @unbrained/pm-cli/sdk/merge entrypoint as a standalone bundle so its public import contract does not eagerly traverse unrelated focused SDK chunks or intermittently exceed the mandatory startup budget under normal host load.
type: Chore
status: in_progress
priority: 1
tags[5]: agent-efficiency,bundling,performance,quality-gate,sdk
created_at: "2026-08-13T11:26:44.669Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-13T11:46:44.352Z"
assignee: "harness:codex"
claim_principal: "harness:codex#3e72d1e1e1b98ee0c323a3b0"
author: "harness:codex"
acceptance_criteria: sdk/merge is emitted as a standalone no-splitting bundle without focused-chunks imports; bundle manifest and package exports remain complete; focused bundle tests and exact SDK import-cost gates pass under the existing threshold; repository coverage remains exactly 100/100/100/100
goal: project management = context management
objective: Keep narrow public SDK entrypoints genuinely narrow at runtime as well as at the type surface.
value: Faster deterministic agent startup and a trustworthy non-flaky mandatory import-cost gate.
impact: Consumers of the merge-only SDK surface load only merge dependencies; CI no longer depends on unrelated focused chunk topology.
outcome: "The emitted sdk-merge.js has no focused-chunks imports, behavior and package exports remain compatible, and the exact import-cost gate passes without raising budgets."
why_now: The broad exact-coverage implementation exposed repeated sdk/merge import-budget failures while an isolated proof bundle reduced median startup materially.
parent: pm-usfg
risk: medium
confidence: high
